        // reason beside it is how a defect becomes expected behaviour.
        //
        // This asserted 50/100 for exactly one commit, to pin the claim that
        // coupling the budget to the frame moved nothing at the then-default. It
        // moved nothing, that commit shipped, and the default then became retail's
        // own 100 ms on evidence: 50 frames per 5 s window measured live, pending
        // mean 6.7 / max 19 against a max of exactly 8 in the run that felt bad,
        // droppedOverflowUserCmds flat at 12 (all inside the world-spawn stall,
        // against 1009 in earlier runs), cmdAge inside the 50 ms runs' own band --
        // and only then the player: "this feels good compared to what i experienced
        // last time. repeated movements left to right actually feel good."
        //
        // CODOL's command loop has no independent time budget. The queue itself
        // is bounded, so zero means process the complete received burst this frame
        // instead of adding one or more frames of delay for a remote client.
        const auto *const frameOverride = std::getenv("OLMOD_SV_FRAME_MS");
